REVISED U DC Amendment toeliminate maximum125%limit on accessory parking.
seek more than the 10%of the required number of parking spaces, the Director may grant
additional parking, with mitigation measures, up to a maximum 125% of the required number.
Currently, Section 6.2.7 of the UDC states: "No Site shall be permitted to provide more than
the Board of Adjustment. This absolute limit has stymied re-use and redevelopment of vacant,
in-fill retail stores and shopping centers.
On December 3rd, the Planning Commission unanimously recommended approval of a text
amendment to grant more flexibility to the Director to approve additional parking.That
amendment was brought to this Committee on December 17th and this Committee Sought to
increase the as-of-right additional parking to 25% of the requirement. At the December 20th
consideration,
What you have before you is a substitute amendmentto the U DC to replace the Section6.2.7
Maximum 125% accessory parking limit with a provision that provides an option for Applicants to
provide parking in excess of the 125%. It also allows up to 25% additional parking as-of-right.
This revision would allow the Director to grant additional parking over the 25% as-of-right
shared parking AND incorporate 2 or more of the mitigating features such as (1) 15% additional
landscape screening of the parking lot:(2) additional open space equal to the square footage of
the additional parking spaces;(3) 5% additional landscaping within the parking lot; or (4) porous
surface of the additional parking spaces.
This revision would also allow the Director to grant additional parking beyond the 125% limit if
